# L1-OUT-003 / L2-WRT-021: the rule covers EVERY record without a Command
# Word, not only a 0x2000 continuation. A standalone SPURIOUS_DATA (0x2001)
# stamped after an equal-timestamp run follows the record that arrived last;
# sorting would move that record (RT3) away from the end, so the run is
# emitted in arrival order: RT20, RT3, spurious.

# RT20 SA11 Receive - clean @ .000500
0224 0F18 20DB F401 7EA1 0004 0000 0000
2F00 22CA 2F00 22CA 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 71C7 0018

# RT3 SA11 Receive - clean @ .000500
0224 0F18 20DB F401 7E19 0004 0000 0000
2F00 22CA 2F00 22CA 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000 0000
0000 0000 71C7 0018

# SPURIOUS_DATA, standalone (preceded by a clean record) -> 0x2001 @ .000501
2005 0F18 20DB F501 0000
